## 3. Tooling note: dbatools

[dbatools](https://dbatools.io) is the de facto community PowerShell module for SQL Server administration and migrations. It handles the SID/password/job-owner mess correctly out of the box. Even if you prefer your own scripts (control, audit trail, no module dependency on locked-down servers), it's worth knowing about:

- `Export-DbaInstance` — exports nearly everything (logins, jobs, linked servers, configs, etc.) to scripted files.
- `Copy-DbaLogin`, `Copy-DbaAgentJob`, `Copy-DbaLinkedServer`, `Copy-DbaCredential`, `Copy-DbaDbMail`, `Copy-DbaResourceGovernor`, `Copy-DbaSysDbUserObject`.
- `Start-DbaMigration` — wraps the whole lot. Read carefully before running.
- `Test-DbaMigrationConstraint` — flags issues that would block.

The manual scripts below give you full visibility into what's being captured. Pick your approach per object type; mixing is fine.

