## 4. PRE-MIGRATION: instance-level capture

### 4.1 Version, edition, build, instance properties

```sql
SELECT
    SERVERPROPERTY('MachineName')               AS machine_name,
    SERVERPROPERTY('ServerName')                AS server_name,
    SERVERPROPERTY('InstanceName')              AS instance_name,
    SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion')            AS product_version,
    SERVERPROPERTY('ProductLevel')              AS product_level,
    SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel')        AS product_update_level,
    SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateReference')    AS product_update_reference,
    SERVERPROPERTY('Edition')                   AS edition,
    SERVERPROPERTY('EngineEdition')             AS engine_edition,
    SERVERPROPERTY('Collation')                 AS collation,
    SERVERPROPERTY('CollationID')               AS collation_id,
    SERVERPROPERTY('LCID')                      AS lcid,
    SERVERPROPERTY('IsClustered')               AS is_clustered,
    SERVERPROPERTY('IsHadrEnabled')             AS is_hadr_enabled,
    SERVERPROPERTY('HadrManagerStatus')         AS hadr_manager_status,
    SERVERPROPERTY('IsFullTextInstalled')       AS is_fulltext_installed,
    SERVERPROPERTY('IsIntegratedSecurityOnly')  AS is_integrated_security_only,
    SERVERPROPERTY('IsAdvancedAnalyticsInstalled') AS is_advanced_analytics_installed,
    SERVERPROPERTY('IsPolyBaseInstalled')       AS is_polybase_installed,
    SERVERPROPERTY('FilestreamConfiguredLevel') AS filestream_configured_level,
    SERVERPROPERTY('FilestreamEffectiveLevel')  AS filestream_effective_level,
    SERVERPROPERTY('FilestreamShareName')       AS filestream_share_name,
    SERVERPROPERTY('ResourceLastUpdateDateTime') AS resource_last_update,
    @@VERSION                                   AS full_version;
```

### 4.2 sp_configure values

```sql
SELECT name, value, value_in_use, minimum, maximum, is_dynamic, is_advanced
FROM sys.configurations
ORDER BY name;
```

Pay particular attention to: `max server memory (MB)`, `min server memory (MB)`, `max degree of parallelism`, `cost threshold for parallelism`, `optimize for ad hoc workloads`, `backup compression default`, `remote admin connections`, `clr enabled`, `Database Mail XPs`, `Ole Automation Procedures`, `xp_cmdshell`.

### 4.3 Trace flags

```sql
DBCC TRACESTATUS(-1);
```

Note this only shows currently-active flags. Permanent flags are set as startup parameters (next section).

### 4.4 Startup parameters (PowerShell, run on the server)

```powershell
# Replace MSSQLSERVER with MSSQL$InstanceName for named instances
$Instance = 'MSSQLSERVER'
$RegPath  = "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Microsoft SQL Server\$Instance\MSSQLServer\Parameters"

Get-ItemProperty -Path $RegPath |
    Select-Object -Property * -ExcludeProperty PS* |
    Format-List
```

Look for `-T` flags (trace flags), `-E` (extent allocation), `-g` (memory_to_reserve), and the master DB file paths.

### 4.5 SQL Server service accounts and startup state (PowerShell)

```powershell
Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_Service -Filter "Name LIKE 'MSSQL%' OR Name LIKE 'SQL%' OR Name = 'MsDtsServer%'" |
    Select-Object Name, DisplayName, StartName, State, StartMode, PathName |
    Format-Table -AutoSize
```

### 4.6 tempdb configuration

```sql
SELECT
    f.name                                 AS logical_name,
    f.physical_name,
    f.type_desc,
    f.size * 8 / 1024                      AS size_mb,
    CASE WHEN f.max_size = -1 THEN -1
         ELSE f.max_size * 8 / 1024 END    AS max_size_mb,
    CASE WHEN f.is_percent_growth = 1 THEN CAST(f.growth AS VARCHAR(10)) + '%'
         ELSE CAST(f.growth * 8 / 1024 AS VARCHAR(10)) + ' MB' END AS growth
FROM tempdb.sys.database_files f
ORDER BY f.type_desc, f.file_id;
```

Capture also: number of data files (target: 1 per logical core up to 8), equal sizing, autogrowth in MB not %, trace flags 1117/1118 superseded by 2016+ default behaviour but worth noting if pre-2016.

