### 10.2 Top queries by total CPU / IO / duration

```sql
SELECT TOP 50
    qs.execution_count,
    qs.total_worker_time / 1000        AS total_cpu_ms,
    qs.total_worker_time / qs.execution_count / 1000 AS avg_cpu_ms,
    qs.total_elapsed_time / 1000       AS total_elapsed_ms,
    qs.total_logical_reads,
    qs.total_logical_writes,
    qs.total_physical_reads,
    qs.last_execution_time,
    DB_NAME(qt.dbid)                   AS database_name,
    OBJECT_NAME(qt.objectid, qt.dbid)  AS object_name,
    SUBSTRING(qt.text, qs.statement_start_offset / 2 + 1,
        (CASE WHEN qs.statement_end_offset = -1 THEN DATALENGTH(qt.text)
              ELSE qs.statement_end_offset END - qs.statement_start_offset) / 2 + 1) AS statement_text
FROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs
CROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_sql_text(qs.sql_handle) qt
ORDER BY qs.total_worker_time DESC;
```

Run three versions: `ORDER BY total_worker_time DESC`, `ORDER BY total_logical_reads DESC`, `ORDER BY total_elapsed_time / NULLIF(execution_count,0) DESC`. Save each.

