## 14. Reconciliation: what to diff

Once you have source and target captures, the ones that *must* reconcile:

| Capture | Tolerance |
|---|---|
| Logins (name + SID + hash) | Zero diff |
| Database list + compat level + recovery model | Zero diff (except deliberate changes) |
| Server role memberships | Zero diff |
| Database users + SID | Zero diff |
| Database role memberships | Zero diff |
| Database-level permissions | Zero diff |
| Agent jobs (name, owner, enabled, steps, schedules) | Zero diff |
| Linked servers (definition + linked logins) | Zero diff (passwords need re-supply) |
| Trace flags + startup parameters | Zero diff (re-apply on new instance) |
| sp_configure values | Match by intention; some defaults change between versions |
| Database file count, sizes, growth | Allowed to differ if intentional |
| TDE state per database | Zero diff |

Diffs are easiest in PowerShell:

```powershell
$src = Import-Csv "C:\Migration\source\logins.csv"
$tgt = Import-Csv "C:\Migration\target\logins.csv"
Compare-Object $src $tgt -Property name, sid_hex, type_desc
```

Or feed both into the same temp table on a third instance and do `EXCEPT` / `INTERSECT` queries — gives you symmetric diffs cleanly.

